B.Lr=new A.br("Goal of battle")
B.LW=new A.c6("You attack on your initiative with fleet and approach allocation. Defenders set Defense Command in advance. The fight resolves in three approaches at once.")
B.La=new A.br("Damage score")
B.LH=new A.c6("Each approach produces a breach share \u2014 how much of that approach\u2019s defense was overcome. The damage score blends all three approaches (Approach One counts most).")
B.L4=new A.br("Winning vs holding")
B.PD=s(["Breakthrough \u2014 damage score above 50%. You may steal Titanium.","Hold \u2014 damage score 50% or below. No Titanium changes hands on that strike."],t.s)
B.K7=new A.cr(B.PD)
B.KT=new A.br("Lane allocation")
B.LF=new A.c6("You may place up to 20 command points of ships across approaches. Defenders place 10 garrison CP independently. Weighting means fleet on Approach One matters most.")
B.KH=new A.nO("Recon improves information quality, not combat power. Battles always use the defender\u2019s real setup and your real fleet.")
B.Lt=new A.br("Strategy, not just rules")
B.M3=new A.c6("Winning commanders predict the defender, then make that prediction wrong. See BEGINNER COMBAT GUIDE and STANCES for playbooks; RECON OPERATIONS for intelligence workflow.")
B.PC=s([B.Lr,B.LW,B.La,B.LH,B.L4,B.K7,B.KT,B.LF,B.KH,B.Lt,B.M3],t.g)
B.Mi=new A.fu("combat-basics","COMBAT BASICS","Learn how battles are won.",B.PC,!1)
B.L8=new A.br("Three steps to win a battle")
B.Rg=s(["Recon \u2014 spend charges to learn doctrine, stance, trap, and lane assessment before you strike.","Identify the prediction \u2014 Fortress bets on where fleet CP lands; Counter bets on which hull carries the most CP.","Make the prediction wrong \u2014 shift lanes or hull mix so their doctrine misses and your hits land harder."],t.s)
B.Kf=new A.cr(B.Rg)
B.KF=new A.nO("Your default attack fleet is not universal. Change composition and approach split to match what recon reveals.")
B.KO=new A.br("As a defender")
B.R0=s(["Set Primary and Secondary stances plus a trap before you are struck.","Use Balanced when intel on attackers is thin; specialize when you expect repeat matchups.","Read COMMON COMBAT MISTAKES before copying someone else\u2019s defense package."],t.s)
B.K6=new A.cr(B.R0)
B.QW=s([B.L8,B.Kf,B.KF,B.KO,B.K6],t.g)
B.Me=new A.fu("beginner-combat","BEGINNER COMBAT GUIDE","Three steps to win a battle.",B.QW,!1)
B.LX=new A.c6("All hulls use the same combat rules: command points, hits, and damage per hit. There is no hidden hull-beats-armor table \u2014 outcomes depend on responses, doctrine, traps, and approach allocation. Within each approach, hits fire in order \u2014 all Frigate hits, then Cruiser, then Battleship.")
B.RD=s(["Class","CP","Pattern","Raw / hull"],t.s)
B.Qg=s(["Frigate","1","3 \xd7 20","60"],t.s)
B.O0=s(["Cruiser","2","1 \xd7 150","150"],t.s)
B.Pk=s(["Battleship","5","1 \xd7 450","450"],t.s)
B.OG=s([B.Qg,B.O0,B.Pk],t.rj)
B.Mv=new A.tU(B.RD,B.OG)
B.L2=new A.br("Frigate")
B.Rt=s(["Role: many small hits \u2014 volume and follow-up after defenses are stressed.","Strengths: can wear down Armor over many events. Strong vs Absorb \u2014 Frigates face the least reduction (~10%). Early Frigate fire can interact with Deflect before larger ships shoot in the same approach.","Weaknesses: poor efficiency vs Armor per CP if Deflect blocks early volleys. Enemy Counter \u2014 Frigates (when their prediction is correct) cuts Frigate damage sharply."],t.s)
B.Kk=new A.cr(B.Rt)
B.KY=new A.br("Cruiser")
B.PQ=s(["Role: solid single-hit damage per CP \u2014 the workhorse against many defenses.","Strengths: efficient vs Armor; strong answer to Deflector-heavy plans when mixed with follow-up hits.","Weaknesses: one Deflect block can negate a Cruiser hit in that approach. Vulnerable to Counter \u2014 Cruisers when the defender prediction is correct."],t.s)
B.Kz=new A.cr(B.PQ)
B.KU=new A.br("Battleship")
B.Qw=s(["Role: Largest individual attacks in the game.","Strengths: Strong against low-hit Flat tiers; efficient 20 CP burst; useful when attack volume stays low.","Weaknesses: Absorptive Matrix reduces Battleship damage most aggressively (~60% band). Deflector can neutralize opening capital strikes. High hit-count Flat tiers punish sustained volume \u2014 not pure capital stacks alone."],t.s)
B.KD=new A.cr(B.Qw)
B.KX=new A.br("Response interactions")
B.Q8=s(["Flat Armor \u2014 Anti-hit-count defense.\n\nMore attacks = stronger armor. The more attacks a fleet generates, the stronger Flat Armor becomes. Designed to suppress high-volume fleets and sustained attack pressure. Low-hit capital fleets remain its natural counter.","Deflect \u2014 Deflector is an anti-opener defense. Excels against low-hit and capital-heavy opening attacks.","Absorb \u2014 ~10% / ~50% / ~60% damage reduction vs Frigate / Cruiser / Battleship attacks (by ship size). Absorptive Matrix is an anti-ship-class defense. Excels against cruiser-heavy and class-concentrated fleets."],t.s)
B.Ka=new A.cr(B.Q8)
B.Rk=s([B.LX,B.Mv,B.L2,B.Kk,B.KY,B.Kz,B.KU,B.KD,B.KX,B.Ka],t.g)
B.Mr=new A.fu("ship-classes","SHIP CLASSES","Frigates, Cruisers, Battleships.",B.Rk,!1)
B.LT=new A.c6("Defenders pick an Initial Response (Primary) and a Trap Response (Secondary). Only one stance is active per battle \u2014 traps swap Primary for Secondary when their condition fires.")
B.Lk=new A.br("Flat Armor")
B.LR=new A.c6("The more attacks a fleet generates, the stronger Flat Armor becomes. Designed to suppress high-volume fleets and sustained attack pressure. Low-hit capital fleets remain its natural counter.")
B.LL=new A.c6('Identity: Anti-hit-count defense.\n\nQuestion answered: "How many attacks is the fleet generating?"\n\nMore attacks \u2192 stronger armor\nFewer attacks \u2192 weaker armor')
B.P4=s(["Mechanism: fleet hits = (Frigates\xd73) + (Cruisers\xd71) + (Battleships\xd71). \u22644 \u2192 20% DR \xb7 5\u20138 \u2192 30% \xb7 9\u201320 \u2192 40% \xb7 21+ \u2192 50%.","Strong when (defender): high hit-count fleets \xb7 frigate swarms \xb7 sustained volume (e.g. F20_C0_B0, F10_C5_B0).","Weak when (defender): low-hit capital fleets \xb7 concentrated burst attacks (e.g. F0_C0_B4).","Attacker playbook: Expect anti-hit-count defenses \u2014 prefer low-hit capital lines (e.g. F0_C0_B4) over frigate swarms (F20_C0_B0, F10_C5_B0).","Defender playbook: Choose Flat Armor when you expect an opponent to generate many attacks. The more attacks a fleet produces, the greater the protection provided by Flat Armor. Against low-hit battleship fleets, its protection is reduced.","Common mistakes: expecting Flat to blunt pure Battleship stacks; feeding high hit-count fleets.","Recon notes: Initial Scan shows Primary; deepen to confirm trap and Secondary before you commit fleet shape."],t.s)
B.Kv=new A.cr(B.P4)
B.Lq=new A.br("Deflector Field")
B.LC=new A.c6(u.o)
B.Pl=s(["Role: anti-opener defense \u2014 disrupts a small number of powerful attacks.","Strong when: the attacker relies on Battleships; the attacker depends on one decisive strike; Deflector is activated against capital-heavy fleets.","Weak when: facing cruiser-heavy pressure; facing mixed fleets; facing sustained follow-up attacks.","Attacker playbook: Confirm Deflector; use low-hit capital or cruiser-heavy follow-up \u2014 not Battleship-only openers without pressure after shatter.","Defender playbook: use Deflector to disrupt capital-led attacks; pair with traps carefully; expect cruiser pressure as the primary counter.","Common mistakes: believing Battleships counter Deflector; pure Battleship stacks without follow-up; treating Deflect like Armor.","Recon notes: wrong stance read is costly \u2014 deepen until stance and trap are confirmed."],t.s)
B.Kq=new A.cr(B.Pl)
B.Ls=new A.br("Absorptive Matrix")
B.LI=new A.c6(u.H)
B.Rs=s(["Role: anti-ship-class defense \u2014 class-based absorption bands.","Strong when: facing Frigate-heavy fleets; long pressure fights; attackers who rely on pure Battleship stacks.","Weak when: frigate-heavy or mixed attacker fleets; balanced pressure after recon.","Attacker playbook: Confirm Absorb; lean on cruiser-heavy or frigate volume per band \u2014 not pure Battleship stacks into burst absorption.","Defender playbook: excellent anti-swarm Primary; strong default when opponents are unknown; Secondary often covers capital fleets via trap.","Common mistakes: believing Battleships counter Absorb; pure Battleship stacks; ignoring trap and Secondary.","Recon notes: deepen until stance and trap are confirmed."],t.s)
B.Kn=new A.cr(B.Rs)
B.PU=s([B.LT,B.Lk,B.LR,B.LL,B.Kv,B.Lq,B.LC,B.Kq,B.Ls,B.LI,B.Kn],t.g)
B.Md=new A.fu("stances","STANCES","Primary, Secondary, and how to fight each response.",B.PU,!1)
B.LS=new A.c6("Transmit Defense Command before you are struck: 10 CP garrison, Initial Response, Trap Response, trap condition, and doctrine.")
B.L6=new A.br("Primary vs Secondary")
B.OO=s(["Initial Response (Primary) \u2014 active when no trap fires or no trap is set.","Trap Response (Secondary) \u2014 replaces Primary on every approach when the trap condition matches the attacker fleet.","Primary and Secondary must differ whenever a trap is armed."],t.s)
B.Kp=new A.cr(B.OO)
B.L7=new A.br("Garrison layout")
B.LK=new A.c6("Split 10 CP across three approaches for local defense strength. Doctrine triggers use attacker fleet CP and hull mix \u2014 not where you stacked garrison.")
B.KG=new A.nO("See DEFENSE DOCTRINES and TRAPS for why to pick each option and how attackers counter them.")
B.QS=s([B.LS,B.L6,B.Kp,B.L7,B.LK,B.KG],t.g)
B.Mk=new A.fu("defense","DEFENSE COMMAND","Garrison, Primary, Secondary, and traps.",B.QS,!1)
B.KS=new A.br("Balanced")
B.PG=s(["Why choose: no prediction \u2014 no reward, no penalty when recon is weak or attackers vary.","Information required: none; default for new defenders and uncertain metas.","When correct: steady fight with no doctrine swing.","When wrong: N/A \u2014 there is no miss penalty.","Typical use: hedge defense, alt accounts, holding Titanium without telegraphing a read."],t.s)
B.Kj=new A.cr(B.PG)
B.Lc=new A.br("Counter (Frigates, Cruisers, or Battleships)")
B.QT=s(["Why choose: punish attackers who always lead with the same hull class.","Information required: recon or pattern recognition on their strike templates.","When correct: the predicted hull class deals much less damage.",u.d,"Typical use: anti-swarm (Counter Frigates), anti-cruiser lines, anti-capital stacks \u2014 only when you will commit to the read."],t.s)
B.Kx=new A.cr(B.QT)
B.Lp=new A.br("Fortress (Approach One, Two, or Three)")
B.Ql=s(["Why choose: punish attackers who dump fleet CP on one approach.","Information required: lane assessment from recon or repeated strikes on the same commander.","When correct: enemy hits on the predicted approach are halved.",u.d,"Typical use: counter one-lane habits \u2014 contest the fortress lane without feeding it your strongest CP."],t.s)
B.Km=new A.cr(B.Ql)
B.Qh=s(["Doctrine","Prediction","If right","If wrong"],t.s)
B.RC=s(["Balanced","None","No modifier","No modifier"],t.s)
B.Qc=s(["Fortress","Most enemy fleet CP on chosen approach","Half damage on that approach","~20% extra damage all hits"],t.s)
B.Ra=s(["Counter","Chosen hull carries most enemy CP","That hull hits much softer","~20% extra damage all hits"],t.s)
